WEBVTT

00:27:59.685 --> 00:28:01.030
I needed a clear picture

00:28:01.054 --> 00:28:04.326
of what empathy had to do
with demand, control, support.

00:28:04.350 --> 00:28:07.676
There's actually evidence that empathy
can contribute to burnout.

00:28:07.700 --> 00:28:10.576
When someone's in pain
and you're unable to help,

00:28:10.600 --> 00:28:12.976
feeling their pain drains you.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.762
This is known to happen to physicians

00:28:14.786 --> 00:28:17.526
who get overwhelmed
by empathy for patients.

00:28:17.550 --> 00:28:21.326
So I asked Adrienne why empathy
has been so powerful.

00:28:21.350 --> 00:28:24.436
AB: Well, let me give you an example, OK?

00:28:24.460 --> 00:28:25.626
Maybe that would help.

00:28:25.650 --> 00:28:28.876
Of a conversation
that I might typically hear.

00:28:28.900 --> 00:28:30.473
This is the doctor talking.